FILE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/integration/review-depth-convergence.vitest.ts
CONTEXT (already implemented, do not change): scripts/reduce-state.cjs `reduceReviewState(specFolder, { write: true, artifactDir })` now builds `registry.dimensionCoverage` with the four canonical keys then each custom name from config `reviewDimensions`; scripts/convergence.cjs `--stop-decision` reads `config.reviewDimensions` and `registry.dimensionCoverage` to compute `missingDimensions` (see `stopDecisionReviewFacts`) and picks `reasonDetail: 'all_dimensions_clean'` when the review is clean (see the `cleanReviewStop` branch).
EDIT: append ONE new top-level `describe('review custom dimension stop path', ...)` block at the end of the file. Model it on the existing `describe('review minIterations floor from loop state', ...)` block in the same file (its `stopDecisionAt` helper shows the namespace, temp dir, config, state log and `runScript('convergence', [... '--stop-decision' ...])` pattern). Differences:
- config `reviewDimensions: ['correctness', 'performance']`, no `antiConvergence` floor, and enough iterations with falling `newFindingsRatio` that the run can stop (copy the floor case's shape; iterations alternate `dimensions: ['correctness']` and `dimensions: ['performance']`).
